The problem with the knights jump location is you need to be
skilled at polearm.  Otherwise you need to be straight on.  The
cost is 3 slots.

> Using a spetum might be a good idea.

Other types of polearm are heavy.  Spetum has the best damage
per weight ratio of any polearm.  Not as much damage as a
halberd but a third the weight.  Even better trolls that get a
weapon get one from a random list of 4 polearm types and spetum
is in that list.  While the first polearm is likely to come from the
mine town watch, face enough trolls and you're nearly assured of
a spetum.

> Though I rarely ever practise this
> type of weapon. Would it be worth spending some skill slots?

A matter of tastes.  There's certain to be one Castle, likely to be
two.  A polearm rules for handling the door of either castle but
has limited application in most other circumstances.

A polearm works if you use your pets as a screening force.
Your pets goes to melee range, you hang out one back poking
at any monster that your pet bites.  Not a strategy that works
for monsters that come in large groups.

As to exercising it, once I've maxed out my luck with the mines
end stone if I'm going to exercise polearm I'll wield it while moving
from level to level.  Explore with main melee weapon and missiles,
relocat among already explored levels by poking monsters along
the path.

> (I supposed
> it depends on the character class played. Cav Kni Pri Ran Sam Val Wiz
> can get skilled in polearms, and Hea Rog Tou basic.)

Very much dependent on class.  If a class can't get to skilled then
there is no advantage to even enhance polearm to basic.  If a class
can get to skilled and thus use the knights jump location for the
castles, it is spending 3 skills slots on the gates of the two castles.
With reflection and MR, standing straight on to the Castle gate or
Ludios isn't that dangerous for your character.

Note that a knight would want to do it with a lance not a spetum if
that knight ever intends to joust.  Lance is much heavier than spetum
but a knight can reach expert and hit adjacent as well as two away.



